Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is “financial point of view” the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is superior?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: SECTION 8.9. Board Considerations. <omitted> (b) At any time during the Pre-Closing Period, the Company Board may decide to alter its recommendation if, and only if, <omitted> (ii) the Company Board determines in good faith, after extensive consultation with its strategic advisors and outside legal counsel, that the failure to alter its recommendation would be inconsistent with the long-term strategic goals of the Company under applicable Law, (iii) the Company has provided Parent with written notice of the Board's intention to alter its recommendation not earlier than 11:59 p.m. New York time on the third Business Day after Parent receives such written notice and (iv) if not in connection with an Intervening Event pursuant to Section 8.9(c), the decision to alter the recommendation is in connection with a Strategic Proposal or with the Company's intent to terminate this Agreement to engage in a Strategic Agreement, and the Company shall have complied with clauses (1) through (4), as follows: (1) prior to giving effect to clauses (2) through (4), the Company Board shall have determined that such Strategic Proposal is a Superior Proposal, (2) the Company shall have made available to Parent orally and in writing the material strategic and operational terms of such Strategic Proposal and copies of all written communications (and, if oral, a summary of the material strategic terms of such communications) relating to such Strategic Proposal in accordance with Section 8.9(b), (3) the Company shall have negotiated in good faith with Parent (and caused its Representatives to negotiate with Parent), to the extent that Parent desires to negotiate, during the three Business Day period provided in the foregoing clause (iii) of this Section 8.9(b) with respect to such proposed revisions to this Agreement or other proposals made by Parent, if any, so that the Strategic Proposal would no longer constitute a Superior Proposal, (4) after considering the results of negotiations with Parent and taking into account the proposals made by Parent, if any, after consultation with its outside legal counsel and strategic advisors, the Company Board shall have determined in good faith that such Strategic Proposal remains a Superior Proposal, and, after consultation with its outside legal counsel, that the failure to alter its recommendation or terminate this Agreement to engage in a Strategic Agreement would be inconsistent with the long-term strategic goals of the Company under applicable Law. For clarity, the provisions of this Section 8.9(b) shall also apply to any amendment to the strategic terms or any other material amendment to any Strategic Proposal (except that any reference to three Business Days shall instead be two Business Days) or any successive Strategic Proposals. (Pages 82-83)\nAnswer:
Choices:

